  "final_answer_preview": "According to Section 61 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023, criminal conspiracy is defined as when two or more persons agree with a common objective to do, or cause to be done, an illegal act (Section 61(1)). Furthermore, anyone who is a party to such a conspiracy is liable under this section (Section 61(2)). An illustration provided in Section 46 demonstrates this concept, where individuals A and C are involved in a conspiracy to poison Z, leading to Z's death, thus implicating C in the conspiracy despite not directly conspiring with A.",
